{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>When you kindle the lamps.</b> When you light the six lamps." "<b>Toward the face of the Menorah.</b> That is, the central shaft; this is when you turn the flame of each of the six lamps toward the central shaft." "<b>The seven lamps shall give light.</b> All seven shall illuminate and bestow supernal light upon Israel, so that they may discern that the light of the lamps on the right and the light of the lamps on the left are directed and turned toward the light of the central shaft, which is the principal element of the Menorah. And so it is fitting: the aim of those on the right, who are engaged in eternal life, and those on the left, who are engaged in temporal life yet assist those on the right — as they said: אִלְמָלֵי עִלָּיָא לָא מִתְקַיְּימֵי אַתְכְּלִיָּא, 'Were it not for the higher ones, the lower ones would not endure' (Ḥullin 92a) — should be to fulfill the will of El, blessed be He, in such manner that His purpose be achieved among all of them together, and that they exalt His name in unison, as they accepted upon themselves, as He testified in saying: וַיַּעֲנוּ כָל הָעָם יַחְדָּו וַיֹּאמְרוּ כֹּל אֲשֶׁר דִּבֶּר ה׳ נַעֲשֶׂה, 'And all the people answered together and said: all that HaShem has spoken we will do' (Exodus 19:8) — that is, all of us together shall fulfill His purpose."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:39:00.989412572Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}